WEBVTT

00:00:00.723 --> 00:00:02.933
Verb tense and verb forms.

00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:07.047
Match the time clues, and make sure every sentence has one main verb.

00:00:08.581 --> 00:00:10.366
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:10.366 --> 00:00:13.496
The choices are one verb in different tenses.

00:00:13.496 --> 00:00:18.330
And the passage has time clues, like dates, since, or by the time.

00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:21.822
It's testing whether the verb fits the timeline.

00:00:22.881 --> 00:00:24.341
Here's the method.

00:00:24.341 --> 00:00:29.346
Hunt for time clues: dates, words like since, and the other verbs.

00:00:29.346 --> 00:00:35.606
Pick the time frame: finished in the past, past up to now, or an even earlier past.

00:00:35.606 --> 00:00:38.786
Check the sentence has one real main verb.

00:00:38.786 --> 00:00:41.522
And keep lists in the same tense all the way through.

00:00:42.631 --> 00:00:46.641
Rule one: a finished past date takes the simple past.

00:00:46.641 --> 00:00:50.206
In nineteen twenty-eight, Fleming has noticed is wrong.

00:00:50.206 --> 00:00:51.126
Fleming noticed.

00:00:52.206 --> 00:00:55.461
Rule two: since means has or have.

00:00:55.461 --> 00:00:58.156
Since nineteen forty-five, the U.

00:00:58.156 --> 00:00:59.126
N.

00:00:59.126 --> 00:01:00.911
expanded is wrong.

00:01:00.911 --> 00:01:02.987
It has expanded, from then up to now.

00:01:04.073 --> 00:01:08.043
Rule three: for an even earlier past, use had.

00:01:08.043 --> 00:01:11.659
By fifteen nineteen, the Aztecs had already built a huge city.

00:01:12.693 --> 00:01:14.178
Let's try one.

00:01:14.178 --> 00:01:16.718
First, hunt for time clues.

00:01:16.718 --> 00:01:23.623
There's a date, eighteen twenty-five, the phrase by the time, and the verb took, which is in the past tense.

00:01:23.623 --> 00:01:26.323
So everything here happens in the past.

00:01:26.323 --> 00:01:28.493
Completes is present tense.

00:01:28.493 --> 00:01:30.398
Will complete is future.

00:01:30.398 --> 00:01:34.538
Has completed connects to the present, not to the eighteen twenties.

00:01:34.538 --> 00:01:38.998
Had completed means finished before a point in the past, which fits.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.109
The answer is C.

00:01:41.173 --> 00:01:43.403
Watch out for has versus had.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.118
Has connects to now.

00:01:45.118 --> 00:01:47.173
Had points to an even earlier past.

00:01:48.214 --> 00:01:55.074
Here's the whole lesson on one page: how to spot it, the four steps, the tense rules, and the trap.

00:01:55.074 --> 00:01:57.959
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
